course: dictionary
lesson: 13590
title: Not quite finished
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: In incompletely, the prefix in- means not, and complete means whole or finished. Put them together and incompletely means not fully finished. Read this: «The painting was left incompletely, with the sky still blank.» The painting is not fully done, because the sky is missing.
explain: Use context to check your meaning. Take «She answered the question incompletely.» Ask yourself: was the answer whole, or were some parts missing? Parts were missing, so incompletely fits. Put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Incompletely is a formal word. You will meet it in science, maths and school reports. In everyday talk, people often say "not fully" or "only partly" instead. Knowing both kinds of word helps you read well and write well.
fact: Incompletely means not fully or not totally, with some parts missing or not finished.
fact: Incompletely is an adverb, because it tells you how something was done.
fact: In maths, a problem solved incompletely is missing some of its steps.
fact: In science, a fuel burned incompletely can make carbon monoxide, which is harmful to breathe.
fact: Homework done incompletely has some parts missing, so check your work before you hand it in.
exercise: «The builders left the wall incompletely built before the storm.» What does incompletely mean here? | Very strong and tall | *Not fully finished | Built in a hurry and very neatly | Painted bright blue
exercise: Sam's maths problem was solved incompletely. What does this tell you? | *Some of the steps are missing | Sam solved it with a red pen | Sam solved it very quickly with a calculator | Sam finished every step
exercise: Which word means about the same as incompletely? | Totally | Loudly | Brightly | *Partly
test: «The cake was baked incompletely, so the middle was still runny.» What does incompletely mean? | Cut into neat pieces | Covered in thick icing | Baked for far too long | *Not fully baked
test: Which picture shows a job done incompletely? | A jigsaw sold in a shop | A jigsaw packed in a box | *A jigsaw with three pieces still missing | A jigsaw with every piece in its place
exam: Why is it dangerous when a fuel burns incompletely? | It makes the fuel heavier | It makes the room too cold to use | *It can make carbon monoxide, which is harmful to breathe | It makes the flames too bright to see
